{
  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-RIEMANN-RECTANGLE-INTERFACE-PRODUCTION-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The classification is not-faithful-weaker. The complete conditional Lean proposition follows from its own explicit and bundled premises, whereas it does not recover the selected source's general conservation and numerical approximation content. Additional restrictions in those premises are reduced applicability, not genuine strength.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target universally binds method and hdomain before introducing any output witnesses. D026 already requires a certified solver and constant-state consistency; D021 and D029 place initial data and D005 conservation inside each solver result. Printed pages 4–5 discuss conservation for discontinuous solutions and numerical fluxes approximating physical fluxes."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The request is resolved by distinguishing the complete conditional proposition from a claim that the source supplies its method or validates its certificate definition. The former is derivable from the supplied structures. The latter is neither asserted by this target nor established by the selected source. The blind translation accurately exposes this distinction.",
      "primary_evidence": "Both elaborated dossiers quantify over an already supplied method. Blind translation hypotheses explicitly include certified solver availability and constant-state consistency. D014, D017, and D026 confirm these are input requirements rather than newly produced guarantees."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The unresolved analytic correspondence does not require an undetermined overall classification here. Lean-implies-source fails on independent substantive grounds, and source-implies-Lean holds for the actual conditional proposition without using any analytic correspondence. Uncertainty about the source's intended shock formulation remains recorded separately.",
      "primary_evidence": "D015, D016, and D026 impose no unequal-state flux approximation relationship. The final existential asserts only equality to D020's update expression. Every required rectangle certificate is already supplied by D017's return type."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The overall relation-strength check fails because exact equality to an unrestricted information-to-flux map does not represent approximation to a correct physical flux. The narrower analytic question remains unresolved: D005 gives locally absolutely continuous interval mass and the derivative balance almost everywhere for each fixed spatial interval, but does not guarantee the displayed derivative identity at every time. This uncertainty is unnecessary for either final implication verdict.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 4, equation (1.10), displays a time derivative; printed page 5 retains integral conservation at discontinuities without specifying exceptional times. D005 instead specifies an integral identity with locally integrable boundary-flux functions. Printed page 5, section 1.2, assigns numerical fluxes an approximation role absent from D016 and the target equalities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The explicit boundary conventions are correct: the initial jump value is unrestricted, cell widths are positive, and oriented integrals accommodate reversed endpoints. The certificate nevertheless imposes a particular representative-sensitive endpoint formulation at every spatial point and all real times, including negative times. Its equivalence with the source's unspecified shock interpretation remains unestablished; it must not be treated as a verified definitional reformulation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.11) specifies only x < 0 and x > 0, exactly as D006 does. D024 ensures positive widths, D027 normalizes by those widths, and D097 defines oriented integrals. D005 universally quantifies x, a, b, s, and t and evaluates physicalFlux at the actual point values of q."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The existence scope of Lean is definite: it assumes a solver on an explicit admitted domain and produces no new method-existence, uniqueness, entropy-selection, or similarity theorem. Its certificates require all-real-time conservation. These requirements restrict applicability; their availability for every source problem is not proved or needed to derive the conditional target. Omitting a universal similarity assertion is appropriate because the source qualifies similarity as typical.",
      "primary_evidence": "D026 requires solve for each problem satisfying domain and includes all equal-state problems. D029 contains only initial data and rectangle conservation. The paragraph after (1.11) uses a qualified similarity description, not an unrestricted well-posedness theorem. The supplied linear method declarations provide a separate linear instantiation, but the target does not specialize method to that construction."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The implication is yes for the complete conditional translation. Set U to D019's normalized averages, choose each solved value by applying method.solve with hdomain, define information and numericalFlux by the supplied maps, and define updatedCellAverages by D020. Grid fields, hintegrable, solver certificates, and the consistency field supply every remaining conjunct. No assumption that equation (1.10) is equivalent to D005 is required. This reasoning concerns declaration types and definitions, not the excluded target proof.",
      "primary_evidence": "D004, D019, D024, and D027 supply the average predicate and adjacency. D017, D021, and D029 supply certified interface solutions. D015 and D016 supply the two maps. D026 supplies the constant-state equality. D020 supplies the final function. The complete elaborated target contains no further obligation."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity and numerical-flux adequacy",
      "resolution": "The hypotheses admit nonconstant intended examples, so there is no global impossibility or empty-state explanation. However, they also admit flux procedures with no meaningful approximation guarantee. For scalar unit-speed advection, use translating Riemann steps and let the extractor return the problem's state pair. A flux map equal to the left state on equal pairs and to the left state plus an arbitrary fixed nonzero constant on unequal pairs satisfies the bundled constant-state condition. Its error against the positive-time physical interface flux persists as unequal states approach equality. Thus satisfiability passes, while numerical adequacy does not follow. The direct judge's C12 failure should be understood as concern about substantive content, not as evidence of inconsistent premises.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1, equations (1.2)–(1.3), gives constant-speed translation. For speed one, q(x,t) is the left state when x < t and the right state when x > t; its positive-time interface flux is the left state. D026 permits extraction depending on the implicit problem and constrains the resulting map only on selected equal-state solver outputs. D005 admits these locally integrable translating steps."
    },
    {
      "item": "Solver-output identity and the scope of the source workflow",
      "resolution": "The statement does not identify its existential solved family with method.solve outputs, and its constant-state consistency conjunct therefore need not govern every permitted existential flux witness. This limits any claim that the target specifies execution of that particular method. However, the source does not prescribe a particular solver, so this missing equality is not independently a decisive source mismatch. The source-level rejection rests on missing physical approximation content and conditional conservation scope.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated conclusion constrains information i by extractInformation (solved i), while constant-state consistency explicitly uses method.solve. D026 has no uniqueness or extractor-invariance requirement. Printed page 5 describes solving the neighboring Riemann problem without identifying a specific solver implementation."
    },
    {
      "item": "Dependency reuse and preserved mathematical conventions",
      "resolution": "The supplied dependency bodies and constructor types support the blind interpretation. Reused logical, real-arithmetic, topology, module, and matrix declarations introduce no hidden approximation, solver identity, or existence guarantee. Fin m represents the intended finite real state dimension; the actual flux derivative is tied to a matrix with a complete real eigenbasis. Normalization, neighboring-state order, and flux orientation are preserved. Global state-space hyperbolicity and all-time certification remain additional input restrictions.",
      "primary_evidence": "D025 ties the Fréchet derivative to Jacobian multiplication; D028 with D113, D114, D136, and D137 supplies a real eigenbasis. D018 uses Q(i−1) and Q(i); D027 divides by cell length; D005 uses left flux minus right flux. D032–D034 are ordinary conjunction, equality, and existence. Their supplied reuse records establish provenance, not task-specific adequacy."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "The conditional target supplies a pipeline for an already certified method but does not constrain unequal-state numerical fluxes to approximate physical interface fluxes or connect the updated sequence to an evolved physical state. The scalar advection construction described above satisfies its premises while permitting a persistent arbitrary interface-flux error. Conservation is supplied by certificates for chosen local solutions, not established for the source's independently considered discontinuous solutions generally. Correct normalization, signs, and Riemann initial data do not recover these missing claims."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the actual Lean binders and bundled premises, choose the canonical normalized cell averages, apply the supplied certified solver at each admitted adjacent pair, and define information, fluxes, and updated values by the supplied functions. All remaining assertions are input properties or certificate projections. The complete conditional proposition therefore follows without using any source theorem. This does not establish that the source guarantees a method with these properties, nor that its instantaneous conservation statement is equivalent to the rectangle predicate."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected source pages do not determine whether conservation at discontinuities means an almost-everywhere derivative balance, a trace formulation, or another weak interpretation. Equivalence with D005's all-endpoint, all-real-time rectangle predicate remains unestablished.",
    "The source gives no quantitative threshold or error metric for a numerical flux to approximate the correct flux reasonably well. No particular accuracy order or bound can be extracted from this passage."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "missing-physical-approximation-relationship",
      "evidence": "Printed page 5 assigns numerical fluxes the role of approximating correct edge fluxes. D015, D016, and D026 permit arbitrary unequal-state outputs, and the final target conjunct only defines updated values through D020.",
      "impact": "The target permits procedures lacking the numerical meaning of the selected source workflow."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "conditional-repackaging",
      "evidence": "D026 already supplies the solver and constant-state consistency; D021 and D029 place initial data and rectangle conservation in its return type. All output families can then be selected or defined from these inputs.",
      "impact": "The theorem does not establish the substantive certificates or their availability in the general source setting. Its additional hypotheses cannot count as genuine strength."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unestablished-analytic-correspondence",
      "evidence": "Equation (1.10) displays an instantaneous derivative balance, while D005 requires rectangle identities and slice integrability at every real endpoint and time. The source's discontinuity discussion does not specify that interpretation.",
      "impact": "The rectangle certificate cannot be accepted as a verified equivalent of the source law. This uncertainty does not obstruct classification of the complete conditional target."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "selected-solver-execution-not-identified",
      "evidence": "The existential solved family is not equated to method.solve, whereas the consistency assertion concerns method.solve specifically.",
      "impact": "The target does not characterize the supplied method's particular execution or transfer its consistency assertion to every permitted existential witness. The source itself does not mandate a particular solver."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "nonvacuity-and-preserved-conventions",
      "evidence": "Positive dimensions, positive adjoining cells, and translating scalar Riemann steps give satisfiable nonconstant instances. D006, D018, D027, and D005 preserve the free jump value, neighboring-state order, normalized average, and left-minus-right conservation orientation.",
      "impact": "Rejection concerns substantive coverage and applicability, rather than inconsistent premises, degenerate division, or incorrect local signs."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source renderings and supplied declaration evidence resolves the classification disagreement without majority vote. The reverse implication is settled by the logical structure of the complete conditional proposition: its own premises supply every needed certificate and function. The forward implication fails because those structures do not express the source's physical approximation relationships or general conservation claim. Analytic ambiguity at shocks remains explicit, but no longer prevents the implication decision. The appropriate classification is not-faithful-weaker. No tools, filesystem access, target proof, or independent hash recomputation were used."
}
